# Sentence halves matching — two columns, click to seat

## Scope

Use this engine for **beginnings ↔ endings** (vocab collocations, reporting verbs, writing purposes, etc.).

**Do NOT use for Listening Part 3** (speakers ↔ A–H). Those pages stay on the classic **options list + `<select>`** pattern — etalons: `unit1-listening/sb-1-1/`, `listening/unit10/fce/telling-lies/`. See `reuse-existing-engines-first.mdc`.

## Hard UX rule (SHM tasks only)

1. **Exactly two columns** on screen: left fixed, right seats already lined up row-by-row. **No** third bank column, **no** empty “drop zone” column.
2. **Primary:** click left **1**, then right **f** → **f swaps** into the seat opposite 1.
3. Also works the other way; optional drag to swap.
4. Do **not** use letter-only badges with a static options list for these SHM tasks.
5. Readable type (~0.95rem). No nested bank scroll.

## Shared engine

| Role | Path |
|------|------|
| Engine | `js/fce-sentence-halves-match-engine.js` → **`FCE_SENTENCE_HALVES_MATCH.mount`** |
| Styles | `css/fce-sentence-halves-match.css` |
| Reference | `unit9-vocabulary/give-collocations-match/index.html` |

Also: `unit9-grammar/reporting-verbs/index.html`, `unit9-vocabulary/give-workbook/index.html` (Ex. 2), `unit1-writing/article/` (Ex. 2 purposes — left = full paragraph text in order).

If A–H has unused letters in an SHM task: add extra `.shm-pair` rows labelled **Not used** so every option stays seated (engine needs equal slots).

**Writing / reading “match purpose”:** left column = the **actual paragraph text** (numbered in book order), right = purpose chips — never labels alone + `<select>`.

## Markup

```html
<div class="shm-pair-head">
  <div class="shm-col-title">Beginnings …</div>
  <div class="shm-col-title">Endings …</div>
</div>
<div class="shm-pairs" id="match-rows">
  <div class="shm-pair" data-line="1">
    <div class="shm-begin">…</div>
    <div class="shm-slot"></div>
  </div>
</div>
<div id="endings-bank" class="shm-endings-box" hidden>
  <button type="button" class="shm-ending" data-letter="a">…</button>
</div>
```

Mount seats bank endings into slots (shuffled). Pairing = which letter sits opposite which line.

## Don’t

- Three-column layouts (begin | empty drop | bank).
- “Drop ending here” labels.
- Separate click engines with badges only.
- **Listening Part 3** pages (use select etalon instead).
